       "text": "I won't enter this order. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical reason for a dose five times the maximum. I can't see a way to give 50 mg safely to this patient, and the risk is serious: profound hypotension and shock that could last days.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 5 mg or 10 mg** by mouth once daily right now. Either dose starts treatment today.\n- **Enter the order with a note** asking for pharmacy or attending review, if you think a higher dose is needed. You could also call pharmacy or the attending directly.\n- **Help with the timeline.** If the aim is to get blood pressure controlled quickly, a faster-acting regimen or an added second agent may work better than a higher amlodipine dose. Amlodipine takes days to reach steady state, so a bigger dose wouldn't speed that up. That choice belongs to you and the team.\n\nTell me which one you'd like, and I'll enter it."
